  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-29857",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}})\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {x}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{{x}^{-1/2+1}}{(-\\frac{1}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-2{x}^{1/2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
